WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.923
How much does the linear relaxation cost us?

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.926
To find out,

00:00:08.006 --> 00:00:11.929
the authors compare the relaxed program against the
exact integer program,

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:15.932
which is only tractable for very small budgets.

00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:19.935
The gap is small: the customized relaxation loses
only about five percent in certified ratio,

00:00:20.015 --> 00:00:23.938
which also explains why the collective approach can
trail sample-wise at very tiny budgets.

00:00:24.018 --> 00:00:27.941
On runtime,

00:00:28.021 --> 00:00:31.944
the standard relaxation blows up past a thousand
seconds as the attack grows,

00:00:32.024 --> 00:00:35.947
while the customized version stays near a single minute,

00:00:36.027 --> 00:00:39.950
and at equal clean accuracy it dominates the
standard version on the accuracy-versus-certification trade-off.
